{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 3, :comments ["<b>And they took from before Moses</b> — Now in a single day they brought all this donation (above, 35:22–29) to the Tent of Meeting, which was Moses' tent, and the wise men took it from before him on that very day and on the next morning. And likewise on the second day they brought yet more donation to him, to his tent, and he commanded to bring it to the craftsmen, until they said to him that the people were bringing in abundance, and it was sufficient and more. And the excess was not a matter of importance enough to be recounted in the portion of Eileh Pekudei — what was done with it — perhaps it was stored in the Tent to reinforce structural needs of the Tabernacle, or to make service vessels from it, as they would do in the Temple with surplus donations (Shekalim 4:4). And Scripture mentioned (Exodus 36:5), \"the people are bringing in abundance,\" to praise the people who bring in their voluntary donation, and to glorify the wise men for their faithfulness, and also the officer over them is praised in this matter, that he had a proclamation passed through the camp to restrain them, for he has no desire for their silver and gold like other rulers over their people, as it says, \"I have not taken one donkey from them\" (Numbers 16:15)."], :book :exodus, :voice :ramban, :lang :en, :chapter 36, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T03:22:02.757021954Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}